#Problem APEX 2.2.12

## DBsubject(Calculus - single variable)
## DBchapter(Applications of differentiation)
## DBsection(Rates of change - natural and social sciences)
## KEYWORDS('units', 'derivative')
## Institution(Valdosta State University)
## Author(S. V. Ault)
## Level(3)
## TitleText1('APEX Calculus')
## AuthorText1('Hartman')
## EditionText1('3.0')
## Section1('2.2')
## Problem1('12')

DOCUMENT();
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'parserPopUp.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

@month = (
    'January',   'February', 'March',    'April',
    'May',       'June',     'July',     'August',
    'September', 'October',  'November', 'December'
);
@num_days = (31, 28, 31, 30, 31, 30, 31, 31, 30, 31, 30, 31);
$index    = random(0, 11);
$day      = $month[$index] . ' ' . random(1, $num_days[$index]);

$length_unit = list_random('feet', 'meters', 'centimeters');

$ans = DropDown(
    [ $length_unit, "hours", "$length_unit/hour", "$length_unit/feet" ], 2);

BEGIN_PGML
The height [`H`], in [$length_unit], of a river is recorded [`t`]
hours after midnight, [$day].  What are the units
of [`H'(t) `] ?

[_]{$ans}

END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION

Since [` H'(t) `] measures the rate of change of [`H`] (in *feet*) with respect to change in [`t`] (in *hours*), the units must be *feet per hour*, or *feet/hour*.
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();
